Subject: [PATCH] planning_head: cast occupancy indices to float before metric conversion

torch.nonzero returns int64. The two assignments below write float results back
into that same int64 tensor, so every occupancy coordinate handed to the collision
optimiser is truncated toward zero. On the 0.5 m BEV grid this displaces every
occupied cell by a mean of 0.5 m -- one full cell -- and always toward the ego
vehicle, because truncation toward zero is toward the grid origin, which is the
ego. Cell (103, 97) reaches the solver at (-1.00, 1.00) m instead of
(-1.25, 1.75) m.

The cast must happen BEFORE the arithmetic. Casting afterwards truncates first
and then converts the already-wrong integer, which is a no-op on the defect.

--- a/projects/mmdet3d_plugin/uniad/dense_heads/planning_head.py
+++ b/projects/mmdet3d_plugin/uniad/dense_heads/planning_head.py
@@
             pos_xy = torch.nonzero(occ_mask[0][cur_t], as_tuple=False)
             pos_xy = pos_xy[:, [1, 0]]
+            pos_xy = pos_xy.to(torch.float64)
             pos_xy[:, 0] = (pos_xy[:, 0] - self.bev_h//2) * 0.5 + 0.25
             pos_xy[:, 1] = (pos_xy[:, 1] - self.bev_w//2) * 0.5 + 0.25
